/// An assignment through a spelling other than the one declared.
///
/// This is the read path's mirror, and it carries the real hazard of the whole
/// family: because neither spelling resolves to the other, nothing stops a
/// program from ending up with two variables where the author meant one.  Note
/// that this file declares the name only once, so it stays a valid test however
/// a duplicate declaration is eventually treated -- see CaseSecondDeclaration.
///
/// Fails with: Undefined variable 'total'.
///
test 'An assignment reaches the variable under any spelling';
begin
    var Total : Integer := 1;

    total := 2;

    AssertEqual (2, Total);
end
